       "type": "example",
       "title": "Tutorial 01. multiple-choice questions: with reasoning",
       "bodyHtml": "<p><b>Q1.</b> Select the correct idea of opportunity cost:</p>\n    <p>(I) Value of the best alternative given up &nbsp;(II) Resources are very limited compared to human requirements &nbsp;(III) Total amount spent on purchase &nbsp;(IV) None of the above</p>\n    \n    \n    \n\n    <p style=\"margin-top:14px\"><b>Q2.</b> Available resources are very limited compared to humans’ unlimited wants. This concept is identified as:</p>\n    <p>Choice · Opportunity cost · Scarcity · None of the above</p>\n    \n    \n    \n\n    <p style=\"margin-top:14px\"><b>Q3.</b> Which statement indicates a <i>positive</i> economic statement?</p>\n    <ul>\n      <li>The government should increase spending on healthcare to improve people’s well-being.</li>\n      <li>The maximum retirement age for government employees should be raised to 70.</li>\n      <li>Sri Lankan inflation rate was last year 6.8%.</li>\n      <li>Income inequality is morally wrong, and the government must redistribute wealth more aggressively.</li>\n    </ul>",
-      "solutionHtml": "<b>Answer: I</b>. Opportunity cost is the value of the <b>next-best alternative sacrificed</b> when a choice is made. Option II defines <i>scarcity</i>, not opportunity cost; option III is simply total expenditure."
+      "solutionHtml": "<p><b>Q1 — Answer: I</b>. Opportunity cost is the value of the <b>next-best alternative sacrificed</b> when a choice is made. Option II defines <i>scarcity</i>, not opportunity cost; option III is simply total expenditure.</p>\n      <p><b>Q2 — Answer: Scarcity.</b> Limited resources relative to unlimited wants is precisely the definition of scarcity, the foundation concept of economics.</p>\n      <p><b>Q3 — Answer: \"Sri Lankan inflation rate was last year 6.8%.\"</b> It is a testable factual claim (positive statement); the other three contain value judgements (\"should\"), making them normative.</p>"
     },
